part.think:
Now write all implementations. I'll use Edit to replace the `// TODO: implement` line in each file. I can do parallel Edits on different files.

Canonical implementations:

Not: `Nand(a=in, b=in, out=out);`
And: `Nand(a=a, b=b, out=nandOut); Not(in=nandOut, out=out);`
Or: `Not(a) Not(b) Nand` or De Morgan with Nand. Canonical: Not(a=a,out=nota); Not(b=b,out=notb); Nand(a=nota,b=notb,out=out);
Xor: canonical book: 
```
Nand(a=a, b=b, out=nandab);
Nand(a=a, b=nandab, out=nand1);
Nand(a=b, b=nandab, out=nand2);
Nand(a=nand1, b=nand2, out=out);
```
Mux:
```
Not(in=sel, out=nsel);
And(a=a, b=nsel, out=an);
And(a=b, b=sel, out=bs);
Or(a=an, b=bs, out=out);
```
DMux:
```
Not(in=sel, out=nsel);
And(a=in, b=nsel, out=a);
And(a=in, b=sel, out=b);
```
Not16: 16 Not gates.
And16, Or16, Mux16: 16 gates each.
Or8Way: tree of Or gates.
Mux4Way16: two Mux16 + one Mux16.
Mux8Way16: two Mux4Way16 + Mux16.
DMux4Way: two DMux: DMux(in=in, sel=sel[1], a=a1, b=b1)? Standard: DMux(in=in, sel=sel[1], a=ab, b=cd)? Actually canonical: first DMux sel=sel[1] gives two outputs; then DMux each with sel[0].
DMux8Way: DMux sel=sel[2] then two DMux4Way with sel[0..1].

